            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Rosa Parks</strong><br>\nRosa Parks was born on February 4, 1913, in Tuskegee, Alabama. She grew up with her mother, brother, and grandparents in Pine Level, Alabama. During her childhood, Rosa experienced racial segregation that was deeply rooted in the South. She attended segregated schools, eventually training at the Alabama State Teachers College for Negroes. Her early experiences with racial discrimination and segregation influenced her later activism.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rosa's Introduction to Civil Rights</strong><br>\nRosa married Raymond Parks in 1932, who was a member of the National Association for the Advancement of Colored People (NAACP). Through her husband, Rosa became actively involved in civil rights issues. She served as a secretary and youth leader for the Montgomery chapter of the NAACP and worked on cases of wrongful accusations against African Americans.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Montgomery Bus Boycott</strong><br>\nOn December 1, 1955, Rosa Parks refused to give up her seat to a white passenger on a Montgomery bus, which was required by the segregation laws of the time. Her arrest sparked the Montgomery Bus Boycott, a monumental event in the Civil Rights Movement. The boycott lasted for 381 days and led to a Supreme Court ruling that segregation on public buses was unconstitutional.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
