          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Rosa's Legacy</strong><br>\nRosa Parks passed away on October 24, 2005, but her legacy endures. She is remembered not only for her role in the Montgomery Bus Boycott but also for her lifelong commitment to civil rights. Her quiet strength and determination continue to inspire generations to fight for justice and equality.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Impact on Society</strong><br>\nRosa's act of defiance and the success of the Montgomery Bus Boycott demonstrated the power of peaceful protest and became a catalyst for other civil rights actions. Her courage helped to galvanize the civil rights movement and prompted nationwide efforts to end racial segregation and discrimination.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Educational Influence</strong><br>\nRosa Parks' story is now a fundamental part of education on American civil rights and social justice. Her life and actions are taught in schools across the United States, ensuring that young people learn about the history of racial discrimination and the importance of standing up for one's rights.</p>\n"
              },
